  about her deeply why would mark want his  body to hook up with a museum tour guide  if he's still in love with his ex-wife  jake's identity wouldn't have an  emotional connection to layla in the  same way that mark would and could have  asked her out while he was in control of  the body when mark blacks out while  fighting those men on the rooftop in  cairo he transitions once again and when  he comes to he's actively stabbing the  older of the two men as he and steven  both accuse each other of brutally  raising the body count it's clear that  neither one of them was responsible for  these particular slangs steven is too  kind and hopeful to straight up murder  people like that and while mark is the  fist of konshu he seems to be more of a  reluctant hero than a willing  participant his main goal is keeping  layla safe from harrow and konchu and  we've heard him plead with stephen to  let him take control of the body in  order to prevent civilian casualties in  contrast the identity shedding blood in  the streets of cairo seems to have no  issue with getting his hands dirty at  the end of episode 4 mark blacks out  once again after being shot and wakes up  in a psychiatric office after fleeing  harrow he finds steven in a hospital  room trapped inside a sarcophagus but  before they run into tower at the  hippogoddis the two moonboys pass yet  another room with a lone sarcophagus  inside this sarcophagus is standing  upright and shaking but unlike when  steven was stuck whoever's inside isn't  screaming to be let out so both of them  pass by without investigating but many  fans including myself began to speculate  that this might be jake because we see  steven and mark get their own separate  physical bodies in the afterlife it  stands to reason that if this is jake he  would have his own body too if moon  knight's third persona was  lock lead inside that red sarcophagus he  could have broken free shortly after  mark and steven met taured possibly  during all the 